From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 09:40:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 36/62] verimark: auto-route transceive_async to BULK on the IT
 (047d:8054)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Routes ALL callers of verimark_transceive_async to the BULK
variant when the underlying device is the IT, by checking the
PID at function entry. The handshake.c sites already dispatch
explicitly via the is_it_variant flag ; this auto-routing covers
every other caller (session.c for the AppData round-trips used
by verify/enroll/identify, plus any future opcode added to the
DT path) without each having to learn about IT.

Without this, the first runtime enroll on the IT failed with
"endpoint stalled or request not supported" — fprintd was running
identify-for-enroll, which calls the session layer, which calls
verimark_transceive_async, which was issuing vendor control
transfers on the IT (no such endpoint) and getting USB STALLs.

The auto-route checks `g_usb_device_get_pid(h->native) ==
VERIMARK_PID_IT` and forwards to verimark_transceive_async_bulk,
releasing the local GTask cleanly (the BULK helper creates its
own). The DT path is byte-for-byte unchanged when PID == 0x00F2.

12 standalone tests still green ; full libfprint build clean.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c
index 8340341..b9f4041 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/transport.c
@@ -489,6 +489,22 @@ verimark_transceive_async(VerimarkUsbHandle *h,
         g_object_unref(task);
         return;
     }
+    /* Auto-route to BULK on the IT (047d:8054). All callers that talk
+     * Tudor opcodes go through this function (verify, enroll, identify,
+     * list, ...) ; routing here means they all just work without each
+     * having to learn about is_it_variant. The IT bypasses the wValue
+     * formula / 8-byte alignment quirks of the DT vendor control framing. */
+    {
+        GUsbDevice *dev = (GUsbDevice *)h->native;
+        if (dev != NULL && g_usb_device_get_pid(dev) == VERIMARK_PID_IT) {
+            g_object_unref(task);   /* release the local task, transceive_async_bulk creates its own */
+            verimark_transceive_async_bulk(h, data, data_len,
+                                            resp, resp_size,
+                                            timeout_ms, cancellable,
+                                            callback, user_data);
+            return;
+        }
+    }
     /* Single-chunk only — multi-chunk fragmentation is the sync path's
      * job, and no observed Tudor opcode exceeds the chunk size. */
     if (data_len > VERIMARK_CHUNK_SIZE) {
